---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { BOT_USER_AGENT } from '../lib/bot';
import { PAGE_CACHE_SECONDS } from '../lib/cache';
import '../styles/doc.css';

// Story 2.5: how Saleaway works, and (in "Our bot") what its bot is. Written for visitors first (plain, benefit-led; the technical
// part is the last section, for store owners). No database query. The old `/contact` address, which the bot's user-agent carries,
// forwards to the "Our bot" part, so its id stays.
Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control', `public, max-age=${PAGE_CACHE_SECONDS}`);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How Saleaway works"
  description="Saleaway checks South African online stores every day and shows you who has a sale on and how big the saving is, so you can spot a good deal without opening twenty tabs."
  path="/about"
>
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="doc">
    <h1>How Saleaway works</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Saleaway checks South African online stores every day and shows you who has a sale on and how big the saving is, so you can spot a good deal
      without opening twenty tabs.
    </p>

    <h2>Three simple steps</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>We check the stores.</strong> Every day we look at each store's sale page, so you don't have to.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>We show you the biggest saving.</strong> "Up to 40% off" is the biggest discount we found on that store's sale page. When we can see a
        sale but not how big it is, you'll see "On sale".
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>You go straight to the store.</strong> Tap a store and its own sale page opens in a new tab. You shop and pay with the store, just like
        always.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Always fresh</h2>
    <p>
      Every store shows when we last checked it, like "Checked today" or "Checked 2 days ago". If a sale looks like it has ended, or we haven't been able
      to check a store for a while, we leave it off the list rather than show you old news.
    </p>

    <h2>Good to know</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Check before you buy.</strong> Discounts change quickly and we read them automatically, so a figure can occasionally be out of date or
        wrong. Always confirm the price on the store's page.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>We're independent.</strong> Saleaway isn't run by, affiliated with or endorsed by any of the stores listed.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The store's content stays with the store.</strong> We show a store's name, a link to its sale page and the discount we found. The
        pictures, product details and prices stay on the store's own site.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="our-bot">Our bot</h2>
    <p>
      A note for store owners. Saleaway reads each store's public sale page with a small, polite program: our bot. It always introduces itself honestly
      as <code>{BOT_USER_AGENT}</code>.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        It asks each store for a few requests a day at most: its sale page, its <code>robots.txt</code> and, for some Shopify stores, their public product
        list.
      </li>
      <li>It obeys <code>robots.txt</code>.</li>
      <li>It never hides who it is and never tries to get round a store's protection.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Prefer not to be listed? Add this to your <code>robots.txt</code> and the bot will leave your store alone:</p>
    <pre>User-agent: SaleawayBot
Disallow: /</pre>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
